    <section class="af__step" :class="isOn(1) ? 'is-on' : ''">
      <div class="af__head">
        <h2>Registration and tickets</h2>
        <p>Leave the tiers empty for one simple free RSVP. Add rows and each gets its own price
          and its own limit — <strong>a price of 0 is a free ticket</strong>, and a blank limit
          means as many as the room allows.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="row">
        <label>Total capacity <span class="af-opt">blank = unlimited</span>
          <input type="number" name="capacity" min="0" step="1" value="{{ row.capacity|default('') }}" placeholder="Unlimited"></label>
        <div></div>
      </div>

    {# ── WHAT HAPPENS AROUND THE TICKET ────────────────────────────────────────
       These columns have been saved by the controller since ticketing shipped and have
       never had a field on this form — so every save silently blanked them. The marker
       below is what makes the panel's absence mean "not shown" rather than "cleared";
       see the note beside `event_extras_posted` in the controller. #}
    {% if refund_missing|default([]) is empty %}
    <input type="hidden" name="event_extras_posted" value="1">

    <details class="event-editor__optional"><summary>Cancellations and refunds</summary>
    <div class="af__head" style="margin-top:26px">
      <h2>Cancellations and refunds</h2>
      <p>What an attendee can do for themselves once they have paid. Off by default: it is your
        event and your money, so nothing here changes unless you set it.</p>
    </div>

      <label class="af-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="self_cancel" value="1"
               {% if row.self_cancel|default(0) %}checked{% endif %}>
        Let attendees cancel their own place
      </label>
      <p class="af-note">With this off, the ticket page shows your contact details instead of a
        cancel button — which is what it does today. With it on, giving a seat up frees it for
        the waiting list immediately.</p>

      <div class="row">
        <label>What comes back
          <select name="refund_mode">
            {% for key, label in refund_modes|default({}) %}
              <option value="{{ key }}" {% if (row.refund_mode|default('none')) == key %}selected{% endif %}>{{ label }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
          </select></label>
        <label>If partial, how much <span class="af-opt">percent</span>
          <input type="number" name="refund_percent" min="1" max="100" step="1"
                 value="{{ row.refund_percent|default(50) }}"></label>
      </div>

      <div class="row">
        <label>Refunds close this long before the event <span class="af-opt">hours · 0 = right up to it</span>
          <input type="number" name="refund_cutoff_hours" min="0" max="8760" step="1"
                 value="{{ row.refund_cutoff_hours|default(0) }}" placeholder="48"></label>
        <div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="af-note">After the cutoff an attendee can still give the seat up so somebody on
        the waiting list can have it — they just get nothing back. Those are two different
        things and this keeps them separate.</p>

      {% if 'refund_policy' not in extras_missing %}
      <label>Refund policy, in your own words
        <textarea name="refund_policy" rows="3" maxlength="1000"
                  placeholder="Shown before anybody buys.">{{ row.refund_policy|default('') }}</textarea></label>
      <p class="af-note">The rule above is what the platform DOES automatically. This is what you
        MEAN, and it is shown on the event page before anybody pays.</p>
    {% endif %}
    </details>

    <div class="af__head" style="margin-top:26px">
      <h2>Before they come</h2>
      <p>Who to contact, when registration shuts, and anything they need to know on the day.</p>
    </div>
      {#
        ── A FIELD WHOSE COLUMN IS NOT THERE YET IS A FIELD THAT LOSES WORK ────

        `extras_missing` names the columns this deployment does not have, and it was
        PASSED AND NEVER READ — so on a deployment that has uploaded this code and not
        yet opened `/__setup/migrate`, every box below drew, accepted an organiser's
        typing, and was dropped on save with nothing to say so. The controller's own
        comment beside the variable states exactly that harm as the reason the variable
        exists, which is what makes it §19's shape rather than a vestige: prose
        promising a protection that no reader delivered.

        Its two siblings were already read — `refund_missing` gates the rule above and
        `design_missing` the ticket section below, with the same sentence. This one was
        left out, and the sweep that would have found it was reading a truncated array.

        Gated per FIELD rather than per section, because these sit among boxes whose
        columns are fine and hiding the lot would take away work somebody can do.
      #}
      {% if extras_missing is not empty %}
        <div style="border:1px solid #ecd9a0;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:6px 0 14px;background:#fffdf5">
          <strong style="font-size:14px">Some of these need one more step</strong>
          <p style="font-size:13px;color:#6b5312;margin:6px 0 0;line-height:1.7">
            These columns are not in the database yet:
            <code>{{ extras_missing|join('</code>, <code>')|raw }}</code>. Run
            <strong>/__setup/migrate</strong> and the boxes for them appear. They are
            hidden rather than shown because anything typed into them would be dropped
            on save without a word.
          </p>
        </div>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="row">
        {% if 'organiser_email' not in extras_missing %}
        <label>Organiser email <span class="af-opt">for questions</span>
          <input type="email" name="organiser_email" maxlength="190"
                 value="{{ row.organiser_email|default('') }}"></label>
        {% endif %}
        {% if 'organiser_phone' not in extras_missing %}
        <label>Organiser phone <span class="af-opt">optional</span>
          <input type="text" name="organiser_phone" maxlength="40"
                 value="{{ row.organiser_phone|default('') }}"></label>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        {% if 'sales_close_at' not in extras_missing %}
        <label>Registration closes <span class="af-opt">blank = when the event starts</span>
          <input type="datetime-local" name="sales_close_at" value="{{ sales_close_input|default('') }}" step="1"></label>
        {% endif %}
        {% if 'waitlist_open' not in extras_missing %}
        <label class="af-check" style="align-self:end">
          <input type="checkbox" name="waitlist_open" value="1"
                 {% if row.waitlist_open|default(0) %}checked{% endif %}>
          Offer a waiting list when a tier sells out
        </label>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {# Phase 7: the public page's Livestream / Recording links (links out, never embeds)
         and its Access section. Coming soon needs no field here: it is every public tier's
         "Sales open at" in the tier editor below (EventSales). #}
      <div class="row">
        {% if 'livestream_url' not in extras_missing %}
        <label>Livestream link <span class="af-opt">where people watch it live</span>
          <input type="url" name="livestream_url" maxlength="500" value="{{ row.livestream_url|default('') }}"></label>
        {% endif %}
        {% if 'recording_url' not in extras_missing %}
        <label>Recording link <span class="af-opt">shown once the event has ended</span>
          <input type="url" name="recording_url" maxlength="500" value="{{ row.recording_url|default('') }}"></label>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {% if 'cover_kind' not in extras_missing %}
      {# DEFAULT-GRAPHICS §4: an event with no image draws a default cover whose tone and
         pattern follow its kind. The organiser picks the kind, never a colour. #}
      <label>Kind of event <span class="af-opt">decides the cover shown when there is no image</span>
        <select name="cover_kind">
          <option value="">Not chosen — an awards ceremony if this event belongs to an award, otherwise community</option>
          {% for k, label in cover_kinds|default({}) %}<option value="{{ k }}"{% if row.cover_kind|default('') == k %} selected{% endif %}>{{ label }}</option>{% endfor %}
        </select></label>
      {% endif %}
      {% if 'spotlight_rank' not in extras_missing %}
      {# EVENTS-INDEX §2: the four slides that open /events. Nothing chosen anywhere → the
         next upcoming events lead instead. #}
      <label>Spotlight on the events page <span class="af-opt">one of the four slides that open /events</span>
        <select name="spotlight_rank">
          <option value="">Not in the spotlight</option>
          {% for n in 1..constant('AfricaGates\\Services\\EventsFront::SPOTLIGHT') %}<option value="{{ n }}"{% if row.spotlight_rank|default(0) == n %} selected{% endif %}>Slide {{ n }}</option>{% endfor %}
        </select></label>
      {% endif %}
      {% if 'access_notes' not in extras_missing %}
      <label>Access <span class="af-opt">one per line — step-free venue, live captions, quiet room</span>
        <textarea name="access_notes" rows="3">{{ row.access_notes|default('') }}</textarea></label>
      {% endif %}
      {% if 'attendee_note' not in extras_missing %}
      <label>Note to attendees <span class="af-opt">joining links, parking, dress code</span>
        <textarea name="attendee_note" rows="3">{{ row.attendee_note|default('') }}</textarea></label>
      {% endif %}

      {# Referral sharing, per event. Not every event can afford to give away a share of
         the gate — a free community night, a partner-funded evening, or one whose margin
         is already committed. Ticked by default, because that is what every event did
         before this box existed. Unticking it stops NEW commission on this event only;
         balances already earned stay owed. #}
      <label class="af-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="referrals_enabled" value="1"
               {% if row.referrals_enabled|default(1) %}checked{% endif %}>
        Pay referral commission on tickets for this event
        <span class="af-opt">members who share their link earn {{ referral_rate_pct|default(10) }}% of what a referred buyer pays</span>
      </label>
    {% endif %}

    {# ── TICKET TIERS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       These are real rows now, not a JSON blob the public page printed as prose. Each
       carries its OWN attendee limit, which is what makes "40 early-bird, 40 standard, in
       a hall of 60" expressible — the event's capacity above is still the ceiling for the
       whole room and is checked on top of every tier's.

       A tier with a price is CHARGED: the registration goes to the gateway and no ticket
       exists until Paystack confirms it. Leave the price at 0 for a free RSVP, which is
       confirmed on the spot. #}
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--cn-line-card);border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:6px;background:#fafcfa" x-data="evRepeater({{ tier_seed|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}, {name:'',price:0,perk:'',cap:'',code:'',colour:'',active:true,sold:0})">
      <strong style="font-size:14px">Ticket tiers <small style="font-weight:400;color:#8a9a9c">(a price of 0 is a free RSVP — leave the list empty for one simple free ticket)</small></strong>
      {% if tier_colour_missing is empty %}
      {# ── WHAT THE COLOURS ARE, ONCE ────────────────────────────────────────
         The six slots resolved against THIS event's accent, so "Warm" is a colour an
         organiser can recognise before choosing it rather than a word they have to guess
         at. Change the ticket accent below and this strip moves with it on the next load —
         which is the whole reason the column stores a slot and not a hex. #}
      <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin-top:10px;
                  padding:8px 10px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--cn-line-card);border-radius:9px">
        <span style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a9a9c">Your colours</span>
        {% for key, sw in tier_palette %}
          <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;font-size:12px;color:#3d4b4d">
            <span aria-hidden="true" style="width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;
                     background:{{ sw.fill }};border:1px solid {{ sw.edge }}"></span>{{ sw.label }}
          </span>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      <template x-for="(r, i) in rows" :key="r.id">
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--cn-line-card);margin-top:10px;padding-top:10px">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap">
            <input type="hidden" name="tier_id[]" :value="r.tid || ''">
            <input type="hidden" name="tier_active[]" :value="r.active ? '1' : '0'">
            {# ── THE LADDER, MOVED ────────────────────────────────────────────
               `sort_order` is written from the POSITION OF THESE FIELDS on save, so these
               two buttons are the entire reordering mechanism — no route, no endpoint, no
               schema change. The row number is shown because "third on the page" is the
               thing being changed, and a pair of arrows with nothing between them gives an
               organiser no way to confirm the move landed where they meant.

               `type="button"` on both, and this is not a style preference: the tier list
               sits INSIDE the event's own <form>, and a <button> with no type defaults to
               `submit`. Without it, nudging a tier down would save and redirect the whole
               event — the same family of fault as the nested <form> that used to eat the
               questionnaire's outcome list, and just as invisible, because saving the form
               is exactly what the page looks like it should do. #}
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="ev-move__n" x-text="i + 1"></span>
            <span style="display:inline-flex">
              <button type="button" class="ev-move" @click="move(r.id, -1)" :disabled="i === 0"
                      :aria-label="'Move ' + (r.name || 'this tier') + ' up'">▲</button>
              <button type="button" class="ev-move" @click="move(r.id, 1)"
                      :disabled="i === rows.length - 1"
                      :aria-label="'Move ' + (r.name || 'this tier') + ' down'">▼</button>
            </span>
            <input name="tier_name[]" aria-label="Ticket tier name" x-model="r.name" maxlength="120" placeholder="Tier (e.g. VIP)" style="width:150px">
            <input name="tier_price[]" aria-label="Ticket tier price in naira" type="number" min="0" step="1" x-model.number="r.price" placeholder="₦ 0" style="width:110px">
            {# THE point of this change. Blank = as many as the room allows. #}
            <input name="tier_capacity[]" aria-label="Seats available at this tier" type="number" min="0" step="1" x-model="r.cap" placeholder="Seats (blank = no limit)" style="width:170px">
            <input name="tier_perk[]" aria-label="What this tier includes" x-model="r.perk" maxlength="500" placeholder="What's included" style="flex:1;min-width:140px">
            <button type="button" @click="rm(r.id)" aria-label="Remove row" style="border:none;background:#fbeaea;color:#a4243a;font-weight:700;border-radius:8px;width:34px;height:34px;cursor:pointer">×</button>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:6px">
            <input name="tier_from[]" aria-label="Sales open at" type="datetime-local" x-model="r.from" style="width:200px" step="1">
            <input name="tier_until[]" aria-label="Sales close at" type="datetime-local" x-model="r.until" style="width:200px" step="1">
            {# A code-gated tier is hidden from the public list and refused without the
               code, which is how a sponsor or speaker allocation stays out of sight
               without needing a second, secret event. #}
            <input name="tier_code[]" aria-label="Access code" x-model="r.code" maxlength="60" placeholder="Access code (optional — hides the tier)" style="flex:1;min-width:180px">
            {% if tier_colour_missing is empty %}
            {# ── THE TIER'S COLOUR ──────────────────────────────────────────
               New field, old mechanism. EventTierPalette has shipped six named slots, a
               separation pass and a WCAG edge guarantee for months, and nothing in the
               admin could write the column — so every tier on the platform was NULL and
               every surface that reads a tier colour fell back to a default. The palette
               was complete, correct, and unreachable.

               It is what colours the dot on the printed ticket AND the selection light on
               the registration card, because both read the same resolver. So this one
               choice is the colour the buyer sees on the page and again on the door.

               A select, not a swatch grid: this sits in a row an organiser fills in while
               thinking about prices, and six coloured targets per tier is a place people
               stop and deliberate. The live dot beside it is drawn by a delegated listener
               in admin.js — the admin CSP has no 'unsafe-inline', so there is no onchange
               here and there must not be. #}
            <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap">
              <span class="sr-only">Tier colour</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" data-tier-dot
                    style="width:13px;height:13px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;
                           border:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.25);background:transparent"></span>
              <select name="tier_colour[]" aria-label="Tier colour" x-model="r.colour"
                      data-ag-do="tier-colour" style="width:150px">
                <option value="">No colour</option>
                {% for key, sw in tier_palette %}
                  <option value="{{ key }}" data-fill="{{ sw.fill }}" data-edge="{{ sw.edge }}">{{ sw.label }}</option>
                {% endfor %}
              </select>
            </label>
            {% endif %}
            <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap"><input type="checkbox" x-model="r.active"> On sale</label>
            <span x-show="r.sold > 0" x-cloak style="font-size:12px;color:#1a6118;font-weight:700"
                  x-text="r.sold + ' sold'"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </template>
      <button type="button" @click="add()" style="margin-top:10px;border:none;background:#eef7ee;color:#1a6118;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;padding:8px 14px;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">+ Add tier</button>
      <p style="font-size:12px;color:#8a9a9c;margin:8px 0 0">
        Prices in ₦. {# Said out loud because the list is NOT sorted by price and looks as
        though it might be: an organiser who puts their premium row first is making a
        deliberate choice, and nothing else on this screen would tell them it had taken. #}
        <b style="color:#3d4b4d;font-weight:600">The order here is the order buyers see</b> — use
        ▲▼ to arrange it. Colour and prominence still follow the price, not the position.
        A tier is never deleted once anything has been sold against it — clearing
        "On sale" takes it off the page and keeps the record straight for the people who bought one.
        {% if row.id is defined %}<a href="/admin/events/{{ row.id }}/tickets" style="font-weight:600">See who is coming →</a>{% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>

    {# Early-bird banner (the promo strip across the top of the event page) #}
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--cn-line-card);border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:6px;background:#fafcfa">
      <strong style="font-size:14px">Early-bird banner <small style="font-weight:400;color:#8a9a9c">(optional — auto-hides after the deadline)</small></strong>
      <label style="margin-top:8px">Banner text<input type="text" name="early_bird_text" value="{{ row.early_bird_text|default('') }}" maxlength="255" placeholder="Save ₦8,000 with Early Bird tickets"></label>
      <div class="row">
        <label>Deadline<input type="datetime-local" name="early_bird_deadline" value="{{ row.early_bird_deadline|when_input }}" step="1"></label>
        <label>Link URL<input type="text" name="early_bird_url" value="{{ row.early_bird_url|default('') }}" placeholder="#tickets or https://…"></label>
      </div>
    </div>

    </section>
